<p dir="auto">On creating a new project, you will be guided through some configuration options:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Desired Name <code>--name=</code> (default: current directory name)</li>
<li>Desired template engine <code>--templateEngine=</code> (<code>hbs</code> or <code>twig</code>; default: <code>hbs</code>)</li>
<li>Desired js compiler <code>--jsCompiler=</code> (<code>ts</code> or <code>js</code>; default: <code>ts</code>)</li>
<li>Using theming feature <code>--themes</code> (default: false)</li>
<li>Using client side templates <code>--clientTpl</code> (default: false)</li>
<li>Including example code <code>--exampleCode</code> (default: false)</li>
<li>Installing nitro-exporter <code>--exporter</code> (default: false)</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">It's possible to pass in these options through the command line:</p>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto"><pre class="notranslate"><code>npx -p yo -p generator-nitro@latest -- yo nitro --name=myproject --templateEngine=hbs --jsCompiler=ts --themes --clientTpl --exampleCode --exporter
